{"repositoryId":1250410005,"availability":"available","full":"Builder106/halberd","name":"halberd","description":"A security guard for AI assistants. It checks every tool an AI tries to use, preventing data leaks and unauthorized commands.","category":"Developer tools","language":"Go","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-05-26T15:48:45Z","updated":"2026-10-19T20:57:21Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://halberd-keep.vercel.app","topics":["agentic-ai","ai-security","go","json-rpc","llm-security","mcp","model-context-protocol","prompt-injection","reverse-proxy","zero-trust"],"demo":"https://halberd-keep.vercel.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:22.114Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:22.114Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:22.114Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T22:20:22.114Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Go"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Useful access, with limits you choose. Halberd checks an AI assistant's tool requests against your policies before letting them through.","You ask an AI assistant to look up ten student records. So far, so useful. But the same database tool can receive a command to erase an entire table. Who checks which request gets through?","Halberd sits between the assistant and its connected tools. You choose the rules: which tools are permitted, which commands are forbidden, and which sensitive values should be removed from responses. Halberd applies those rules as requests and responses pass through it."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Builder106/halberd/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"3a994a2561231af6d6034dc88879d2003e6544f1cde3b2c8e36f13e2455d494b","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:22.212Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T22:20:22.212Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Useful access, with limits you choose. Halberd checks an AI assistant's tool requests against your policies before letting them through.","so